{"id": "sevt_01N1Be7MRTBjkij8RZ2g1csf", "content": [{"text": "**Checkout p99 regression from `a3f9c21`: the refactor replaced one batched `order_items` query with a query per open order.**\n\n**Deploy timing (runbook step 2)**\n- Deploy `a3f9c21` (checkout, alice@shop.io) finished at 14:31:18.\n- checkout p99 was steady at about 55\u201377 ms through 14:31, then jumped to 347 ms at 14:32 and reached 852 ms at 14:33. It peaked at 3.6 s at 14:40 and stayed in the 2\u20133.5 s range through 15:00.\n- The only other deploys in the 6h window are cart (09:14), auth (11:02) and inventory (14:55, after the p99 onset), so none of them lines up with the spike.\n\n**Diff**\n- Before: one `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=order_ids)` query, grouped in memory.\n- After: a loop that runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=order.id)` once per open order. The commit message says it is only a readability refactor, but it changes the query count.\n\n**Log confirmation**\n- `order_items` queries first appear at 14:31:18, the deploy time. There are none before it.\n- The log has 30,964 per-order `order_items` queries across 2,586 requests, a median of 12 per request and a maximum of 16.\n- Per-minute volume runs at about 600\u20131,260 queries from 14:31 onward. The batched `IN (...)` form never appears in the log after the deploy.\n\n**Not explained**\n- The error rate rose from about 0.1% to 0.1\u20130.2% starting at 14:40, eight minutes after the p99 jump. I did not trace that lag. It may be timeouts under the slow path, but that is unconfirmed.\n- The inventory deploy at 14:55 came after both onsets, so it does not explain either one.\n\n**Suggested next steps (not run)**\n- Roll back `a3f9c21` or restore the batched query. Then confirm p99 returns to about 60 ms.\n- Check `db_pool_utilization` on checkout to see whether pool exhaustion is adding to the latency or the errors.\n\n**Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the refactor turned a single batched `order_items` lookup into one query per open order, so each checkout summary request now issues about 12\u201316 extra DB round trips and its latency grows with the number of open orders.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T12:02:40.811706Z", "type": "agent.message"}
